# Extra packages for the desktop edition, copied into
# config/package-lists/desktop.list.chroot by auto/config. The desktop itself
# (compositor, shell, portals) comes from the fellowship-desktop .deb that
# desktop/build.sh makes.

# Wayland session and software rendering. QEMU's virtio-gpu has no 3D of its
# own, so the desktop draws through llvmpipe; on real hardware the same Mesa
# package picks the GPU driver.
libegl-mesa0
libgl1-mesa-dri
libglx-mesa0
xkb-data
dbus
# chvt: the session switches the screen to its own console, which the live
# image's autologin does not necessarily leave active
kbd

# Portals: the frontend, and the GTK backend for the file picker and friends.
# The Settings (colour-scheme) interface is answered by fellowship-portal.
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk

# Sound: PipeWire with WirePlumber, and the Pulse-compatible socket the
# media apps reach for. fellowship-session starts all three; the volume
# keys and the top bar speak to them through wpctl (in wireplumber).
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
# notify-send: the small client every desktop has for scripts and tests.
libnotify-bin

# Look: fonts, icons and pointer the shell and the apps ask for.
# DejaVu alone leaves whole scripts with no glyphs, measured on the seat
# 2026-11-15: Arabic renders (DejaVu covers it), CJK draws tofu boxes and
# emoji has no colour glyphs. Noto core is 42 MB across 2 packages and the
# colour emoji font 11 MB in 1. `fonts-noto-cjk` (91 MB) is the one that
# fixes the CJK tofu, and that is a size decision rather than an obvious
# yes.
fonts-dejavu-core
fonts-noto-core
fonts-noto-color-emoji
adwaita-icon-theme
breeze-icon-theme
breeze-cursor-theme

# The folders a desktop is expected to have. Nothing else creates them in
# this session: Debian's own hook sits in /etc/xdg/autostart, which the
# compositor deliberately does not read until FellowshipOS ships its own
# system autostart, so `fellowship-session` runs the updater at login. The
# screenshot path reads the file this writes, and Nemo's sidebar and
# Rhythmbox's library assume the folders exist.
xdg-user-dirs

# The everyday apps chosen in the desktop checklist: GTK 3 where there is a
# choice, so the session's GTK theme reaches them.
foot
mousepad
nemo
ristretto
atril
engrampa
qalculate-gtk
mpv
chromium
rhythmbox
zenity
